> 8. I think there is a strong lack of scrolls of identify in the game.
> Only in a few games I was lucky enough, that the first few shops were
> of the "bookstore"-type and that I could buy identify scrolls.
> But most of the time I find myself accumulating tons and tons of rings
> amulets and gems, hoping that at one point I will be able to find out
> what they are and actually benefit from them. I think not being able
> to use magic items misses the whole point of RPGs. How do you guys
> tackle this?

As others have said, you can identify identify easily enough without 
reading it. Once you know what identify is, never read an identify scroll 
unless it is blessed. (Do you know about blessing objects, and in 
particular how to make enough of the appropriate substance?)

On average, 5 identify scrolls is enough to get you a long way if they are 
blessed.

Rings and amulets can be put on without too many bad effects if they are 
uncursed and you are careful. Some will auto-identify themselves.

Gems can be identified easily if you are an archaeologist or a gnome with 
an archaeologist's equipment. Other players may need a blessed item to do 
this although even an uncursed one can distinguish gems from glass.

